
-steps to deply the mern stack apppication to the aws 

-launch the ec2 instance
-login with the ubuntu or whatever server you chose
-(this time tht linux we chose is ubuntu)

------------------------------------------------------
 ubuntu 
 sudo apt update 
 mkdir mern-todo
 cd mern-todo
 mkdir backend (we ae making another folder in the mern-todo folder)
 cd backend (imp , make sure to check the directory)
 sudo apt install npm (later check , node -v , npm -v)
 npm init -y (inside the backend folder)
 npm install express mongoose dotenv cors
 do ls and see

 nano server.js (creating the file inside the backend folder) (//copy paste the server.js code here & save)

 nano .env (paste the mongourl (which you got from the mongodb))
 
 node server.js (//starts the backend at the given port , in our case it's 5000 , make sure the security groups to these ports 3000& 5000 are available)

 //btw package.json in backend add "type: module" or just copy paste th package.json file  
